    <string name="privacy_text" translatable="false">NetPulse Privacy Policy\n\nWhat the app reads: cell tower information (operator, cell ID, signal), SIM and network type, GPS location, and data usage counters. This is needed to show network measurements.\n\nWhere it is stored: only on your phone — in the app\'s own storage. Drive-test logs (CSV) and cell names never leave your phone unless you share them yourself.\n\nWhat is sent over the internet:\n• Map tiles are downloaded from OpenStreetMap / OpenTopoMap servers (they see your IP address and the map area you view).\n• Only if you add an OpenCelliD API key: the serving cell\'s MCC, MNC, LAC/TAC and cell ID are sent to opencellid.org to find the tower location.\n• Addresses are looked up with Android\'s built-in geocoder (provided by Google on most phones).\n\nNo ads, no analytics, no accounts. No personal data is sold or shared.\n\nDeleting data: clear the app\'s storage or uninstall the app.\n\nContact: open an issue on the app\'s GitHub page.</string>
